From 32038f72357d77d2d4b574060ce1bcfdb93c73e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shikanime Deva <william.phetsinorath@shikanime.studio>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 22:12:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rpc : serve each client connection on its own thread
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ggml_backend_rpc_start_server serves clients from a single accept loop: it
accepts one socket, runs rpc_serve_client to completion, then accepts the
next. In router mode each model child holds a long-lived RPC connection for
the model's lifetime, so the first loaded model permanently occupies the
loop and every later model starves in the kernel accept backlog — its
HELLO is never answered and the child blocks in recv(8) forever. Any
second long-lived connection wedges; it only looks MoE-shaped because a
dense model usually loads first.

Serve each connection on its own detached thread. rpc_server is already
constructed per connection inside rpc_serve_client, so per-connection state
is isolated; the shared backends handles are the same objects the serial
loop already used. Verified with a two-client repro: client A holds its
connection, client B's HELLO returns in 0.00s with this change and never
returns before it.

Signed-off-by: Shikanime Deva <william.phetsinorath@shikanime.studio>
---
 ggml/src/ggml-rpc/ggml-rpc.cpp | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-rpc/ggml-rpc.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-rpc/ggml-rpc.cpp
index c24caad77..c615e2aa3 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-rpc/ggml-rpc.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-rpc/ggml-rpc.cpp
@@ -2141,8 +2141,10 @@ void ggml_backend_rpc_start_server(const char * endpoint, const char * cache_dir
         }
         printf("Accepted client connection\n");
         fflush(stdout);
-        rpc_serve_client(backends, cache_dir, client_socket);
-        printf("Client connection closed\n");
+        std::thread([backends, cache_dir, client_socket]() {
+            rpc_serve_client(backends, cache_dir, client_socket);
+        }).detach();
+        printf("Client connection accepted for serving\n");
         fflush(stdout);
     }
     rpc_transport_shutdown();
-- 
